1
00:00:02,270 --> 00:00:03,830
Previously on "Final Space,"

2
00:00:03,860 --> 00:00:05,210
Gary journeys to Inner Space
to see the titan,

3
00:00:05,240 --> 00:00:07,140
Bolo, who's been asleep
for 10,000 years.

4
00:00:07,170 --> 00:00:09,490
While there, Gary's father
tells him to go to Earth

5
00:00:09,520 --> 00:00:11,250
to find the last
anti-matter bomb.

6
00:00:11,280 --> 00:00:13,530
With it, they can
close Final Space.

7
00:00:13,560 --> 00:00:15,320
Let's hope there's still time.

8
00:00:15,360 --> 00:00:17,080
Hey! Is that mustache Gary?

9
00:00:17,120 --> 00:00:18,570
It sure is.

10
00:00:21,220 --> 00:00:22,710
H.U.E.: Gary.

11
00:00:22,740 --> 00:00:25,400
The cookies will be done
in one minute.

12
00:00:25,430 --> 00:00:27,370
Gary: Oh, good.

13
00:00:27,400 --> 00:00:30,060
I'm extremely excited...

14
00:00:30,090 --> 00:00:33,370
for these cookies.

15
00:00:33,410 --> 00:00:34,550
I'm scared, H.U.E.

16
00:00:34,580 --> 00:00:36,070
I know, Gary.

17
00:00:36,100 --> 00:00:38,070
You'll stay with me
till the end?

18
00:00:38,100 --> 00:00:41,350
Till the very end.

19
00:00:41,380 --> 00:00:43,730
Thank you, H.U.E.

20
00:00:43,760 --> 00:00:46,940
It's been an honor
to be your friend.

21
00:00:51,390 --> 00:00:59,990
♪♪

22
00:01:00,020 --> 00:01:08,410
♪♪

23
00:01:08,440 --> 00:01:17,110
♪♪

24
00:01:19,140 --> 00:01:21,970
Little Caton:
Gary, what were your
father's exact instructions?

25
00:01:22,010 --> 00:01:25,110
He said, "Get the Anti-Matter
bomb and close the breach."

26
00:01:25,150 --> 00:01:27,810
Did he say where
on Earth the bomb is?

27
00:01:27,840 --> 00:01:30,500
In New York.
The one on Earth.

28
00:01:30,530 --> 00:01:31,850
That's a really big place.

29
00:01:31,880 --> 00:01:33,950
Gary, I might be able to help.

30
00:01:33,990 --> 00:01:36,230
I have found this
in your father's files.

31
00:01:36,260 --> 00:01:41,130
Log 2845B --
Captain John Goodspeed.

32
00:01:41,170 --> 00:01:44,690
Big day. Took forever,
but we finally got there.

33
00:01:47,480 --> 00:01:49,140
The Anti-Matter bomb.

34
00:01:49,170 --> 00:01:50,760
What we do here
could be the difference

35
00:01:50,800 --> 00:01:52,280
between Earth's survival

36
00:01:52,310 --> 00:01:54,590
and its being swallowed up
into Final Space.

37
00:01:54,630 --> 00:01:57,150
Hey, John,
if we survive this,

38
00:01:57,180 --> 00:02:01,120
what do you say we kick it up
with some taquitos, bro?

39
00:02:01,150 --> 00:02:03,530
I'm going to kill him.

40
00:02:03,570 --> 00:02:06,670
I know where that is.
It's the Infinity Guard Spire.

41
00:02:06,710 --> 00:02:09,680
Then next stop --
thatplace!

42
00:02:09,710 --> 00:02:11,990
♪♪

43
00:02:16,680 --> 00:02:18,720
[ Beeping ]

44
00:02:18,750 --> 00:02:21,170
Oh, my gosh!
H.U.E., wh-- what is going on?

45
00:02:21,210 --> 00:02:23,170
-Where are we?!
-Earth, Gary.

46
00:02:23,210 --> 00:02:24,830
It has shifted
from its coordinates

47
00:02:24,860 --> 00:02:26,730
and is being sucked
into the breach.

48
00:02:26,760 --> 00:02:28,730
The oceans are the first to go.

49
00:02:28,760 --> 00:02:31,180
Oh, my God.
It's happening.

50
00:02:31,220 --> 00:02:32,460
I blame KVN.

51
00:02:32,490 --> 00:02:33,870
Way to go, KVN. Way to go!

52
00:02:33,910 --> 00:02:35,290
I'm getting better!

53
00:02:35,320 --> 00:02:38,010
You're getting worse.
So much worse! It hurts!

54
00:02:38,050 --> 00:02:39,500
It hurts me physically!

55
00:02:39,530 --> 00:02:41,020
♪ Things are getting better

56
00:02:41,050 --> 00:02:44,330
♪ The sun is shining,
the clouds are parting ♪

57
00:02:44,370 --> 00:02:48,200
♪ And this guy is making
great striiides ♪

58
00:02:48,230 --> 00:02:50,200
Sing with me!
You're doing great, KVN.

59
00:02:50,230 --> 00:02:52,340
Thanks!
I am doing great!

60
00:02:52,370 --> 00:02:53,510
Oh, my God!

61
00:02:53,550 --> 00:02:56,240
That's different.

62
00:02:56,270 --> 00:02:57,480
Turtles?!

63
00:02:57,520 --> 00:02:58,860
That's a little one!

64
00:02:58,900 --> 00:03:00,210
Dear Heavenly Lightning Lord!

65
00:03:00,240 --> 00:03:03,110
We're being attacked
by Ninja Sea Turtles!

66
00:03:03,140 --> 00:03:06,110
No, Gary. But we have flown
into a school of them.

67
00:03:06,150 --> 00:03:08,770
[ Laughs ] Good!
They're still in school.

68
00:03:08,800 --> 00:03:10,700
[ Bang ]
Chookity.

69
00:03:10,740 --> 00:03:12,330
This is so wrong.

70
00:03:12,360 --> 00:03:13,950
This is very wrong.

71
00:03:17,470 --> 00:03:18,950
New York.

72
00:03:18,990 --> 00:03:21,580
The planet has been
mostly abandoned, Gary.

73
00:03:21,610 --> 00:03:25,370
Look at this place.
I've been to New York before.

74
00:03:25,410 --> 00:03:27,440
And this...

75
00:03:27,480 --> 00:03:31,140
This looks better. Not by much.

76
00:03:31,170 --> 00:03:32,720
Gary, uh-oh.

77
00:03:32,760 --> 00:03:36,940
You'll have six hours to locate the Anti-Matter bomb.

78
00:03:36,970 --> 00:03:42,040
After that, all of what
you see now will be gone.

79
00:03:42,080 --> 00:03:45,390
[ Whirring, pulsating ]

80
00:03:45,940 --> 00:03:48,460
The Infinity Guard
betrayed the human race.

81
00:03:48,500 --> 00:03:51,430
They chose their side,
and we're on the other.

82
00:03:51,470 --> 00:03:56,400
They will show us no mercy,
so I suggest we show them none.

83
00:03:56,440 --> 00:03:58,580
Now let's find that bomb.

84
00:03:58,610 --> 00:04:01,270
I have no idea what
you're talking about, but...

85
00:04:01,310 --> 00:04:03,380
Count. Me. Out!

86
00:04:03,410 --> 00:04:05,830
Later! [ Laughs ]

87
00:04:05,860 --> 00:04:07,310
Gary, the S.A.M.E.S.

88
00:04:07,350 --> 00:04:09,830
have retrofitted
the plasma torches, rail guns,

89
00:04:09,870 --> 00:04:11,730
and other sundry
maintenance equipment

90
00:04:11,760 --> 00:04:14,560
into heinous super weapons.

91
00:04:14,590 --> 00:04:17,110
Yes, H.U.E.!
Good lord, yes!

92
00:04:17,150 --> 00:04:18,560
Do you know what
that makes you?

93
00:04:18,600 --> 00:04:21,190
That makes you Employee
of the freaking Month.

94
00:04:21,460 --> 00:04:23,780
[ Buzzer ]

95
00:04:24,330 --> 00:04:26,990
Quinn, can I ask you
something?

96
00:04:27,020 --> 00:04:31,440
Soldier: Fire!Oh, my -- That came kinda fast!

97
00:04:31,470 --> 00:04:33,960
Take 'em out, boys!

98
00:04:33,990 --> 00:04:35,340
Mooncake: Cookity pok!

99
00:04:35,370 --> 00:04:37,620
[ Guns blasting ]

100
00:04:37,650 --> 00:04:39,790
Go, go, go, go!

101
00:04:39,830 --> 00:04:41,970
[ Laughs ] Oh!

102
00:04:42,000 --> 00:04:48,700
[ Guns blasting ]

103
00:04:48,730 --> 00:04:52,150
Quinn, I still have
that question.

104
00:04:52,180 --> 00:04:54,840
Yeah!
Boku!

105
00:04:58,090 --> 00:05:00,470
Mooncake: Woop! Pah!

106
00:05:00,500 --> 00:05:01,680
Gary: Go, Mooncake!

107
00:05:01,710 --> 00:05:05,020
Oh, oh, yes! Yes!
Oh, my -- oh, no.

108
00:05:06,920 --> 00:05:10,170
Quinn! About that question.

109
00:05:10,200 --> 00:05:11,650
What I wanted to ask
is would you like

110
00:05:11,690 --> 00:05:15,000
to drink alcoholic liquids
out of a cup with me?

111
00:05:15,030 --> 00:05:18,000
Now?
You're asking me this now?

112
00:05:18,040 --> 00:05:21,520
Oh, okay, just gonna
cartwheel away from me.

113
00:05:24,420 --> 00:05:27,180
Okay, that was close!
Oh, my God. Ow, ohh! Oh!

114
00:05:27,220 --> 00:05:30,190
But just, you know,
I mean, come on, Quinn.

115
00:05:30,220 --> 00:05:32,360
It jus-- it's just a drink.

116
00:05:32,400 --> 00:05:34,400
Shouldn't we be
concentrating on this?

117
00:05:34,430 --> 00:05:37,500
I can't concentrate on this
because all I am thinking about

118
00:05:37,540 --> 00:05:38,850
is if you wanna go out with me!

119
00:05:38,890 --> 00:05:39,850
Then no.

120
00:05:39,890 --> 00:05:42,370
[ Alarm blaring ]

121
00:05:42,410 --> 00:05:44,240
Die! Die!
Die! Why?

122
00:05:44,270 --> 00:05:46,820
Because I can't concentrate
on killing these guys

123
00:05:46,860 --> 00:05:50,070
if I'm concentrating
on that!

124
00:05:50,100 --> 00:05:51,380
Did anyone ever tell you

125
00:05:51,420 --> 00:05:53,870
emergency lighting
brings out your hotness?

126
00:05:53,900 --> 00:05:55,250
Shut up.

127
00:05:55,280 --> 00:05:56,520
[ Guns blasting ]

128
00:05:56,560 --> 00:05:59,530
♪♪

129
00:06:02,560 --> 00:06:09,290
♪♪

130
00:06:09,330 --> 00:06:11,540
[ Guns blasting ]

131
00:06:11,570 --> 00:06:13,020
Aah!

132
00:06:13,060 --> 00:06:15,720
Ohhh, don't worry, Gary.
KVN can handle this.

133
00:06:15,750 --> 00:06:17,270
KVN, don't handle this.

134
00:06:17,300 --> 00:06:18,790
Handle this?
You got it!

135
00:06:18,820 --> 00:06:21,380
[ Crash ]

136
00:06:23,930 --> 00:06:25,280
[ Rockets soaring ]

137
00:06:25,310 --> 00:06:26,550
[ Explosion ]

138
00:06:26,590 --> 00:06:28,970
[ Whirring, beeping ]

139
00:06:29,000 --> 00:06:30,450
KVN, what the freak is that?

140
00:06:30,490 --> 00:06:33,420
You just had a mech suit
lying around this whole time?!

141
00:06:33,460 --> 00:06:35,870
Yeah, so?

142
00:06:35,910 --> 00:06:39,430
[ Grunting ]

143
00:06:39,460 --> 00:06:42,910
Good lord, I hate you
so feverishly.

144
00:06:42,950 --> 00:06:45,120
It hurts. It physically
hurts me, KVN.

145
00:06:45,160 --> 00:06:46,570
Exo suit KVN: Hey, look, KVN!

146
00:06:46,610 --> 00:06:49,650
-Hey, guys!
-Hey, KVN.
-You look great.

147
00:06:49,680 --> 00:06:51,580
-Hey, KVN.
--What?
KVN, it's me -- KVN.

148
00:06:51,610 --> 00:06:53,130
-What?
-Who?
-Me?
-You!

149
00:06:53,170 --> 00:06:54,580
-Hey, KVN.
-Hey, look, it's KVN.

150
00:06:54,620 --> 00:06:56,170
-Hey, KVN, you look great!
-Hi, KVN! You look great!

151
00:06:56,200 --> 00:06:58,930
Hey, KVN, over here!
Where? Here! Haha!

152
00:06:58,970 --> 00:07:01,930
Don't shoot us --
shoot them.

153
00:07:01,970 --> 00:07:03,450
-Anything for a KVN!
-Anything for a KVN!

154
00:07:03,490 --> 00:07:06,460
-Anything for a KVN!
-Anything for a KVN!

155
00:07:06,490 --> 00:07:07,460
Handled!

156
00:07:07,490 --> 00:07:10,630
Gary,
give him a little something.

157
00:07:10,670 --> 00:07:12,320
How little?

158
00:07:12,360 --> 00:07:14,770
A thumbs up?

159
00:07:14,810 --> 00:07:17,090
Ugh. So much hurt.

160
00:07:17,120 --> 00:07:19,680
My thumb -- It's burning.
[ Cracks ]

161
00:07:19,710 --> 00:07:22,610
Oh! [ Screams ]

162
00:07:22,640 --> 00:07:24,090
We're best friends now.

163
00:07:24,130 --> 00:07:25,820
Guys, do you hear this?
We're best friends now.

164
00:07:25,850 --> 00:07:27,370
We're not even friends.

165
00:07:27,410 --> 00:07:29,720
Right. We're bestfriends.

166
00:07:32,650 --> 00:07:34,480
Gary, there isn't much time.

167
00:07:34,520 --> 00:07:37,310
Only four more hours
to locate the bomb

168
00:07:37,350 --> 00:07:39,800
before the Earth
is sucked into the breach.

169
00:07:39,830 --> 00:07:41,630
Bomb vault, yo!

170
00:07:41,660 --> 00:07:43,010
We found it, guys.

171
00:07:43,040 --> 00:07:44,320
[ Zaps ]

172
00:07:47,010 --> 00:07:49,390
[ Beeping, hissing ]

173
00:07:52,570 --> 00:07:55,850
It's gone. Where is it, H.U.E.?
We're running out of time.

174
00:07:55,880 --> 00:07:57,330
Odds are that space douche

175
00:07:57,370 --> 00:07:59,990
has instructed his
dickheads to hide it.

176
00:08:00,030 --> 00:08:01,610
H.U.E., can you find it?

177
00:08:01,650 --> 00:08:03,030
Mm-hmm.

178
00:08:03,060 --> 00:08:06,790
Hmmm. Ah. All files
have been deleted.

179
00:08:06,830 --> 00:08:10,660
Location unknown.Unknown?!

180
00:08:10,690 --> 00:08:13,630
Then it's over.

181
00:08:13,660 --> 00:08:15,210
Drop your weapons!

182
00:08:15,250 --> 00:08:16,660
Drop them now!

183
00:08:16,700 --> 00:08:18,910
Chookity!

184
00:08:18,940 --> 00:08:21,010
I mean...now it's over.

185
00:08:21,050 --> 00:08:22,810
I thought that --
I thought before we were over,

186
00:08:22,840 --> 00:08:25,530
but now we are
all going to die.

187
00:08:25,570 --> 00:08:26,920
Get down on the floor!

188
00:08:26,950 --> 00:08:30,060
Not that you asked,
but this is why you're single.

189
00:08:30,090 --> 00:08:33,720
I didn't ask. But since you
brought it up, enlighten me.

190
00:08:33,750 --> 00:08:36,930
Okay, well, I actually didn't
think that far ahead, but...

191
00:08:36,960 --> 00:08:39,440
Look, Gary, why do you
even like me?

192
00:08:39,480 --> 00:08:41,860
Because you're
everything I'm not.

193
00:08:41,900 --> 00:08:43,730
And that's
a good thing, right?

194
00:08:43,760 --> 00:08:45,170
Hell, yeah, it is.

195
00:08:45,210 --> 00:08:47,210
Guard: Commencing executions.

196
00:08:47,250 --> 00:08:50,250
Guard 2: Take the life form
to the Lord Commander.

197
00:08:50,280 --> 00:08:53,390
Just a second, guys.
Uh, look, love isn't a formula.

198
00:08:53,420 --> 00:08:55,910
It's messy.
It's real. It's raw.

199
00:08:55,940 --> 00:08:58,390
Prepare to die, traitor.

200
00:08:58,430 --> 00:08:59,530
Then, yes.

201
00:08:59,570 --> 00:09:02,360
I'll drink liquids
with you out of a cup.

202
00:09:02,400 --> 00:09:06,580
[ Laughs ]
I guess one drink can't hurt.

203
00:09:06,610 --> 00:09:07,890
Say goodbye.

204
00:09:07,920 --> 00:09:09,540
[ Zap, zap ]

205
00:09:11,750 --> 00:09:14,450
Sorry I'm late.
Tribore!

206
00:09:14,480 --> 00:09:15,690
Is it Tribore?

207
00:09:15,720 --> 00:09:17,620
It is!

208
00:09:17,660 --> 00:09:19,070
Pachu. Pachu.

209
00:09:19,110 --> 00:09:21,250
Pachu. Pachu. Pachu.

210
00:09:21,280 --> 00:09:23,280
Take five and call me
in the morning.

211
00:09:23,320 --> 00:09:25,460
Hey, guy! I don't know
who you are,

212
00:09:25,490 --> 00:09:28,220
but I like how you keep shooting
people even after they're dead.

213
00:09:28,250 --> 00:09:31,700
Isn't he great?
He's so handsome.

214
00:09:31,740 --> 00:09:33,600
Then welcome
to the Resistance.

215
00:09:33,640 --> 00:09:35,950
Pay attention.
He's talking.

216
00:09:37,640 --> 00:09:38,990
Quick, follow me.

217
00:09:39,020 --> 00:09:40,610
Will it be dangerous?

218
00:09:40,640 --> 00:09:43,750
You bet'cha!

219
00:09:43,790 --> 00:09:45,170
Chookity!

220
00:09:45,200 --> 00:09:46,750
What are you doing here?!

221
00:09:46,790 --> 00:09:49,510
When the Lord Commander
infiltrated the Infinity Guard,

222
00:09:49,550 --> 00:09:53,590
a Resistance rose up
and they needed a leader.

223
00:09:53,620 --> 00:09:56,450
Someone pure of spirit
and incorruptible.

224
00:09:56,490 --> 00:10:00,460
Only one person
met those criteria.

225
00:10:00,490 --> 00:10:02,600
Tribore.

226
00:10:02,630 --> 00:10:04,810
I thought you've just been
skulking around my apartment

227
00:10:04,840 --> 00:10:06,010
wearing my dresses.

228
00:10:06,050 --> 00:10:07,460
I was in deep cover.

229
00:10:07,500 --> 00:10:09,950
Do I have to explain
myself to you? I don't.

230
00:10:09,980 --> 00:10:12,370
Is that my scarf?It was.

231
00:10:12,400 --> 00:10:14,780
Does this Resistance
of yours happen to know

232
00:10:14,820 --> 00:10:16,780
where an Anti-Matter bomb is?

233
00:10:16,820 --> 00:10:18,370
Not yet.

234
00:10:18,410 --> 00:10:20,960
Richard? Hack into
the mainframe.

235
00:10:20,990 --> 00:10:23,310
We need to find
an Anti-Matter bomb.

236
00:10:23,340 --> 00:10:25,860
This way!Shannon: This is amazing.

237
00:10:26,480 --> 00:10:28,800
So this is the end
of the world.

238
00:10:28,830 --> 00:10:30,180
I was hoping for more.

239
00:10:30,210 --> 00:10:32,010
Richard said there
was a secret base

240
00:10:32,040 --> 00:10:34,110
where the bomb is being kept.

241
00:10:34,150 --> 00:10:35,840
That's so Richard.

242
00:10:35,870 --> 00:10:37,460
Do you want to get a drink?

243
00:10:37,490 --> 00:10:38,630
Oh, wait. You're busy.

244
00:10:38,670 --> 00:10:40,460
Why would you want
to get a drink with me?

245
00:10:40,500 --> 00:10:42,260
Just looking
at you is enough...

246
00:10:43,710 --> 00:10:45,190
...for a lifetime.

247
00:10:45,230 --> 00:10:47,990
This is the bar
where we first met!

248
00:10:48,020 --> 00:10:49,300
The entrance is hidden.

249
00:10:49,330 --> 00:10:51,580
How do I know?
I actually don't know.

250
00:10:51,610 --> 00:10:53,960
Come on, KVN.
I need your sensors.

251
00:10:53,990 --> 00:10:55,960
I have sensors?!
Hooray for KVN!

252
00:10:56,000 --> 00:10:58,720
Gary, I have sensors! Yay!

253
00:10:58,760 --> 00:11:00,520
Oh, I can't believe it.
Look -- I can't believe it...

254
00:11:00,550 --> 00:11:03,970
So, are you going to buy me
that drink or what?

255
00:11:04,000 --> 00:11:06,560
Hell, yeah, I am.
Pick your poison.

256
00:11:07,010 --> 00:11:08,420
[ Glasses clink ]

257
00:11:09,590 --> 00:11:11,040
[ Seat squeaks ]

258
00:11:13,770 --> 00:11:19,400
So, I guess, I'm just saying,
this is our first date.

259
00:11:19,430 --> 00:11:20,500
I'm gonna die!

260
00:11:20,540 --> 00:11:23,540
We're entering
the meaningless void!

261
00:11:23,570 --> 00:11:25,230
Cheers.

262
00:11:25,270 --> 00:11:28,060
Civilization ends now!

263
00:11:28,100 --> 00:11:31,100
Glass clink.

264
00:11:31,130 --> 00:11:33,550
Did Tribore find it?
He did!

265
00:11:33,580 --> 00:11:37,660
No thanks to Richard,
which, again, is so Richard.

266
00:11:38,900 --> 00:11:40,660
[ Buzzing ]

267
00:11:44,910 --> 00:11:47,010
[ Door creaks ]
Aah!

268
00:11:47,050 --> 00:11:50,740
No freaking way.

269
00:11:50,770 --> 00:11:54,740
Five years ago I karate chopped
this man to steal his clothes.

270
00:11:54,780 --> 00:11:56,430
Schwa!

271
00:11:59,610 --> 00:12:01,230
Swallow!

272
00:12:01,270 --> 00:12:03,890
You're a good guy, Gary!

273
00:12:03,930 --> 00:12:06,240
Did not anyone help him?!

274
00:12:06,270 --> 00:12:08,550
Oh, you jerk face.

275
00:12:08,580 --> 00:12:09,900
He's still alive.

276
00:12:09,930 --> 00:12:12,040
I gave him aspirin --

277
00:12:12,070 --> 00:12:14,760
No, I gave him Crylenol.

278
00:12:14,800 --> 00:12:16,800
Oh, and I overdosed him.

279
00:12:16,830 --> 00:12:19,110
You're not a good guy, Gary.

280
00:12:19,150 --> 00:12:21,810
Oh, you're such
a terrible human being!

281
00:12:21,840 --> 00:12:25,670
KVN, are you detecting
anything worth chatting about?

282
00:12:25,710 --> 00:12:27,120
Nope. Nope.

283
00:12:27,160 --> 00:12:31,120
Ooh, I mean yes!

284
00:12:31,160 --> 00:12:34,330
Announcer:
Secret underground bathroom
base now accessible.

285
00:12:34,370 --> 00:12:35,610
Tight!

286
00:12:37,920 --> 00:12:39,650
Gary, there is a reinforced
concrete structure

287
00:12:39,680 --> 00:12:42,520
17 meters below the surface.

288
00:12:42,550 --> 00:12:44,000
Not to be a buzzkill,

289
00:12:44,030 --> 00:12:45,690
but the breach's effect
on the Earth

290
00:12:45,730 --> 00:12:47,930
is reaching critical mass.

291
00:12:51,350 --> 00:12:53,490
Gary, would you stop
making the face

292
00:12:53,530 --> 00:12:54,940
and hurry up?

293
00:12:59,700 --> 00:13:07,020
♪♪

294
00:13:07,060 --> 00:13:14,200
♪♪

295
00:13:14,240 --> 00:13:21,380
♪♪

296
00:13:21,420 --> 00:13:28,010
♪♪

297
00:13:28,040 --> 00:13:29,630
♪♪

298
00:13:29,670 --> 00:13:34,020
Gary, I am detecting very high
levels of Anti-Matter.

299
00:13:34,050 --> 00:13:36,050
Tribore.
You did an okay job.

300
00:13:36,090 --> 00:13:38,850
It was nice work.
It was!

301
00:13:38,880 --> 00:13:42,960
Gary: The bomb's in there.
You guys, stay back.

302
00:13:42,990 --> 00:13:44,750
I'm goin' in to get it.

303
00:13:44,780 --> 00:13:47,300
Ah, uh, aah!

304
00:13:47,340 --> 00:13:49,170
Run!Careful, Gary!

305
00:13:51,790 --> 00:13:53,760
[ Click, hiss ]

306
00:13:55,420 --> 00:13:58,350
Structural collapse
imminent.

307
00:13:58,380 --> 00:13:59,590
Get out!

308
00:13:59,630 --> 00:14:01,150
If I get you home by nine,

309
00:14:01,180 --> 00:14:03,700
what are my chances of getting
some lip-to-lip action?

310
00:14:03,730 --> 00:14:06,910
I'm gonna go with moderate.Moderate?

311
00:14:06,940 --> 00:14:09,220
Oh good lord,
my slacks are tightening.

312
00:14:09,260 --> 00:14:11,190
Settle down, Cowboy.

313
00:14:11,220 --> 00:14:13,360
Wahwahwahwahwahwah.Aah.

314
00:14:18,300 --> 00:14:20,750
♪♪

315
00:14:22,650 --> 00:14:24,860
Gary --
What's up?

316
00:14:26,790 --> 00:14:28,900
This is actually
a pretty good first date.

317
00:14:28,930 --> 00:14:34,420
[ Rumbling ]

318
00:14:34,450 --> 00:14:36,080
Ugh!

319
00:14:36,110 --> 00:14:38,180
Quinn!

320
00:14:38,220 --> 00:14:40,600
Quinn!!

321
00:14:40,630 --> 00:14:41,810
Little Cato!

322
00:14:41,840 --> 00:14:43,260
Get this back
to the ship, Spider Cat.

323
00:14:43,290 --> 00:14:45,190
you got it,
Thunder Bandit.

324
00:14:45,220 --> 00:14:48,300
Gary, you do not have the
required speed to reach Quinn

325
00:14:48,330 --> 00:14:49,920
before the pressure kills her.

326
00:14:49,950 --> 00:14:51,130
Who said it was
just going to be me?

327
00:14:51,160 --> 00:14:52,920
Mooncake, double time it!Chokity!

328
00:14:52,960 --> 00:14:57,310
Chok chok chok chok
chok chok chok chok!

329
00:14:57,340 --> 00:14:58,550
H.U.E.! Distance.

330
00:14:58,580 --> 00:15:00,030
130 feet.

331
00:15:00,070 --> 00:15:02,930
Approaching crush depth.

332
00:15:02,970 --> 00:15:04,310
I can see her light.

333
00:15:04,350 --> 00:15:06,380
I would advise you
to go no further.

334
00:15:06,420 --> 00:15:08,940
Seeing as I know
you won't listen to me...

335
00:15:08,970 --> 00:15:12,730
hurry.

336
00:15:12,770 --> 00:15:14,490
H.U.E., what is this?

337
00:15:14,530 --> 00:15:16,320
I am detecting
high levels of magma

338
00:15:16,360 --> 00:15:18,570
about to break through
the Earth's crust.

339
00:15:18,600 --> 00:15:22,090
Oh, no...

340
00:15:22,120 --> 00:15:23,850
Mooncake! Triple time!

341
00:15:23,880 --> 00:15:25,330
Oh, no!

342
00:15:27,540 --> 00:15:29,340
Aah! Aah!

343
00:15:33,720 --> 00:15:35,690
Activate gravity boots!

344
00:15:35,720 --> 00:15:43,320
♪♪

345
00:15:43,350 --> 00:15:50,770
♪♪

346
00:15:50,810 --> 00:15:58,370
♪♪

347
00:15:58,400 --> 00:16:05,860
♪♪

348
00:16:05,890 --> 00:16:07,200
H.U.E.!
Where are you going?

349
00:16:07,240 --> 00:16:10,210
Don't worry,
we will not leave Gary.

350
00:16:10,240 --> 00:16:20,040
♪♪

351
00:16:20,080 --> 00:16:22,050
Go, go, go, go, go, go,
go, Mooncake! Go!!

352
00:16:22,080 --> 00:16:23,870
Ohhh, go, go, go, go, go!

353
00:16:23,910 --> 00:16:26,220
Wa-ehhhhh --

354
00:16:26,260 --> 00:16:27,530
Chokity!!

355
00:16:27,570 --> 00:16:31,020
♪♪

356
00:16:31,050 --> 00:16:33,130
[ Laughs ]

357
00:16:33,160 --> 00:16:34,540
It's not that impressive.

358
00:16:34,570 --> 00:16:35,820
♪♪

359
00:16:35,850 --> 00:16:42,070
Mooncake,
there you are.

360
00:16:43,620 --> 00:16:46,930
♪♪

361
00:16:46,970 --> 00:16:53,840
♪ If only I could fix
the sky... ♪

362
00:16:53,870 --> 00:16:56,670
No, no, no, no, no. No.

363
00:16:56,700 --> 00:16:57,600
H.U.E.!

364
00:16:57,630 --> 00:17:03,050
♪♪

365
00:17:03,090 --> 00:17:09,680
♪ It's got a way of knowing
when to hurt me ♪

366
00:17:09,710 --> 00:17:14,930
♪ Oh, it's when
the night is long ♪

367
00:17:14,960 --> 00:17:17,340
♪♪

368
00:17:17,380 --> 00:17:20,550
Where am I? I remember...
I was in the bathroom.

369
00:17:20,590 --> 00:17:24,450
I had zippered
my pants, and then...

370
00:17:24,490 --> 00:17:27,900
Oh, my God! Aah!

371
00:17:27,940 --> 00:17:30,490
Oh God! Okay...

372
00:17:31,980 --> 00:17:34,530
You jerk!
You jerk face!

373
00:17:34,570 --> 00:17:39,950
♪ Earthquakes break and
shatter the perfect design ♪

374
00:17:41,990 --> 00:17:44,130
Gary?
You're back.

375
00:17:44,160 --> 00:17:45,370
Thought I lost you.

376
00:17:45,400 --> 00:17:46,960
Where are we?
Currently...

377
00:17:46,990 --> 00:17:50,310
well, uh, we're being
yanked into space.

378
00:17:50,340 --> 00:17:54,450
♪ Towers rise to meet
and hear its laughter ♪

379
00:17:54,480 --> 00:17:57,240
Maybe it's because my head
is in the clouds --

380
00:17:57,280 --> 00:17:59,110
Not gonna laugh
at that one, okay. Ha.

381
00:17:59,140 --> 00:18:00,660
I was hoping
for a laugh there --

382
00:18:00,700 --> 00:18:03,490
Would you perchance want
to join forces with me

383
00:18:03,530 --> 00:18:05,110
on a daily basis?

384
00:18:05,150 --> 00:18:07,630
I'm gonna give that
a hard maybe.

385
00:18:07,670 --> 00:18:10,640
I'll take it!
Are you hearing this, Earth?

386
00:18:10,670 --> 00:18:13,710
We're hard maybes! Yes!!

387
00:18:18,710 --> 00:18:24,060
♪ Ohh, oh, oohhh

388
00:18:26,270 --> 00:18:29,860
♪ Ohh, oh, oohhh

389
00:18:29,900 --> 00:18:33,210
[ Screaming ]

390
00:18:34,320 --> 00:18:39,560
♪ Ohh, oh, oohhh

391
00:18:42,190 --> 00:18:47,360
♪ Ohh, oh, oohhh

392
00:18:50,750 --> 00:18:53,540
♪ Ohh, oh, oohhh

393
00:18:53,580 --> 00:18:56,130
H.U.E.! Set a course
for the breach.

394
00:18:58,100 --> 00:19:03,720
♪ Ohh, oh, oohhh

395
00:19:06,000 --> 00:19:11,080
♪ Ohh, oh, oohhh

396
00:19:11,110 --> 00:19:15,180
This could have been so easy.

397
00:19:15,220 --> 00:19:21,570
But time and time again,
you chose the harder path.

398
00:19:21,600 --> 00:19:23,670
The darker path.

399
00:19:23,710 --> 00:19:29,580
It's time for you to see that
your choices have consequences.

400
00:19:29,610 --> 00:19:37,690
I will give you one last chance
to hand over Mooncake.

401
00:19:41,970 --> 00:19:43,690
Chookity.

402
00:19:43,730 --> 00:19:45,110
Hell. No.

403
00:19:45,140 --> 00:19:46,870
He is one of us.

404
00:19:46,900 --> 00:19:48,250
I don't really know him.

405
00:19:48,290 --> 00:19:51,080
But he seems very popular.

406
00:19:52,770 --> 00:19:54,710
He stays with us.

407
00:19:54,740 --> 00:19:56,020
Never.

408
00:19:56,050 --> 00:19:58,090
Then death it is!

409
00:19:58,120 --> 00:19:59,950
I'm coming for you.

410
00:19:59,990 --> 00:20:04,680
Ah, yes, I've seen
that face before.

411
00:20:04,720 --> 00:20:06,440
The face of loss.

412
00:20:06,480 --> 00:20:08,510
We have the
Anti-Matter bomb!

413
00:20:08,550 --> 00:20:11,620
We will close the breach --
you will die!

414
00:20:11,650 --> 00:20:15,140
[ Laughs ]

415
00:20:15,170 --> 00:20:17,730
I look forward to it.

416
00:20:19,560 --> 00:20:21,970
I'm detecting
the approach of an armada

417
00:20:22,010 --> 00:20:24,800
of heavy incinerators.

418
00:20:24,840 --> 00:20:26,120
Everyone's gonna die.

419
00:20:26,150 --> 00:20:27,460
You aren't wrong.

420
00:20:27,500 --> 00:20:30,150
They'reall going to die.

421
00:20:30,190 --> 00:20:33,570
If he wants a war,
he's got one.

422
00:20:33,610 --> 00:20:35,160
Let's do this.

423
00:20:39,850 --> 00:20:44,000
♪♪

424
00:20:44,030 --> 00:20:46,270
♪♪
